      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's solve linked puzzles with three numbers.\n\nThe clues may give pairwise sums, ratios or relationships between the numbers.\n\nThe safest method is to label each equation clearly and use the overlap between them.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If three numbers are added in pairs, add all three equations.\n\n(x+y)+(y+z)+(x+z)=2(x+y+z).\n\nSo the sum of the three pair-sums is twice the total of the three numbers.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
